    'Mena\'s Palace (French Quarter)':
      "A French Quarter diner the Infatuation singles out, a longtime local breakfast-and-po'boy spot with a hot-sausage sandwich worth seeking out.",
    "Walker's BBQ (New Orleans East)":
      "A New Orleans East specialist famous for its cochon de lait po'boy, the slow-roasted-pork sandwich that wins Jazz Fest every year. A Time Out pick.",
    "Verti Marte (French Quarter)":
      "A 24-hour French Quarter corner deli beloved for its overstuffed 'All That Jazz' po'boy and round-the-clock service. A Time Out pick and Quarter institution.",
