      "A beloved Mid-City corner bar with a jukebox, strong pours, and a genuinely local crowd, a regular on the city's dive-bar lists.",
    "Pete's Out in the Cold (Irish Channel)":
      "An Irish Channel hole-in-the-wall PUNCH recommends, the kind of cash-and-character bar that locals guard jealously.",
    'The Saint (Lower Garden District)':
      "A Lower Garden District late-night dive with a photo booth, a punk jukebox, and a reputation as one of the city's great after-hours holes.",
    "Kajun's Pub (Marigny)":
      "A 24-hour Marigny karaoke dive on St. Claude, a chaotic, beloved late-night institution where the singing never really stops.",
    'Lots a Luck Tavern (Navarre)':
      "A Navarre neighborhood tavern Where Y'at ranks among the city's best dives, an unpretentious local where everyone knows the bartender.",
    "Ms. Mae's (Uptown)":
      "The legendary Uptown corner bar at Magazine and Napoleon, famous for absurdly cheap drinks and a come-as-you-are crowd at any hour. A classic NOLA dive.",
