    'Arpège (7th Arr.)': "Alain Passard's vegetable-forward three-Michelin-star institution in the 7th, now fully plant-based since July 2025. Vegetables, herbs, and flowers from the chef's own farms are the centerpiece of one of the longest-running three-star menus in Paris.",
    'Hakuba (1st Arr.)': "Cheval Blanc Paris's hidden 8-seat sushi counter, where chef Toshihiko Yamashita serves a strict edomae omakase. Time Out's best sushi pick for 2026 with one of the highest Google ratings of any Paris counter.",
    'Épicure (8th Arr.)': "Arnaud Faye's three-Michelin-star Le Bristol dining room is the grand summer terrace of Parisian fine dining, opening onto the hotel's French formal garden. Refined classical French cuisine in a setting that defines belle-époque opulence.",
    'Mokochaya (11th Arr.)': "A modern Asian neo-bistro on rue Saint Bernard where chef Kohei Bando blends Japanese technique with French produce. Le Fooding 2026 Best Brunch and a Time Out top 10 pick for 2026.",
    'Recoin (Belleville, 20th Arr.)': "An unfussy Belleville neighborhood bistro doing wine-bar small plates and chalkboard daily specials. Time Out called it the city's #2 restaurant for 2026 in its Best Bistro slot.",
